<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index fell three points to 1,280.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index fell three points to 1,280.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates fell to 1,280 today from 1,283 on June 20, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p> Route Index     Rate   Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1    1362    12.363	  1365    12.394</p>
<p>   1a   1290  9769.000	  1300  9844.000</p>
<p>   2    1506    21.519	  1507    21.525</p>
<p>   2a   1503 12325.000	  1507 12356.000</p>
<p>   3    1333    12.294	  1333    12.300</p>
